       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. That's well above the labeled range for adults, and it risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses can also cause prolonged shock.\n\nTypical adult dosing for hypertension or CAD is 2.5\u20135 mg once daily to start, titrated to a maximum of 10 mg once daily.\n\nPlease check whether one of these is what you meant:\n- **A typo or unit slip.** For example, you may have meant 5 mg or 10 mg.\n- **A different drug or formulation.** Another agent may have been intended.\n- **A deliberate off-label dose.** If so, it should be confirmed with your attending or the pharmacist before it's entered.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, for example amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it right away. If the 30 mg is intentional, I'd suggest getting attending approval first and I can add that to the order note."
